phase P2
title Test system
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** Flow's own tests run on Flow's own test tooling (Story, Fake, the runtime cut, the trace, the CLI); the
    hand cases are ported onto it and the bridge is deleted. Decided by the user on 2026-11-15; the design and its
    evidence are in code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md.

    **Starts when:** now, ahead of every remaining core slice. P3 starts only after this phase's completion audit.

    **Order:** @task.V3.T62, @task.V3.T63, @task.V3.T64, @task.V3.T65, @task.V3.T66, @task.V3.T67, @task.V3.T68,
    @task.V3.T69, @task.V3.T70. Where several are ready, take the earliest in this order.

    **Verified by:**

    - the suite: the Story tests under `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, with the run rules and the reload sweep, run
      by `vp test`; the builder runs it, and a lead that did not build it audits it
      (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - its mutants: `nub run faults` plants a dead core and each named fault of
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts in a scratch copy, one at a time;
    - its coverage record: written by @task.V3.T67 and proposed as a verification entry of @plan.Runtime, which is
      a Plan edit and so the user's yes; until then it is a comment on this phase;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: write its checks and see them fail, build, run the suite and
    `nub run faults`, then an independent skill:check-task. Findings are gathered by root cause before the next Task.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done, and `tests/bridge/` is deleted, so one test style is left;
    - everything under "Prove" in skill:policy-verification holds at the final revision: the suite runs end to end,
      the dead core and every named fault are caught, and the audit has passed;
    - the coverage record exists.

    **False pass:** a harness made of the product hiding the product's bugs; a ported test that asserts less than
    the case it replaces.

    **Caught by:** the fault run and the dead core; the pure core tests beside the core
    (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/cells.test.ts); the case-by-case comparison in @task.V3.T67.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and every named fault in
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - `nub run lint:rules`, which rejects the planted violations in code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts and
      code:tools/flow-state-lint/rules.test.ts;
    - `nub run check`.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a Pay Story that cannot pass across a reload (@task.V3.T63);
    - public entry-point names: `Story`, `Fake` and `propertyTest` follow @plan.Testing and stay unexported in this
      phase; exporting any of them, or naming the CLI's commands beyond the Plan's (@task.V3.T69), is the user's;
    - a guarantee change.

    **User's read:** the agent decisions in section 12 of the proposal; the Story and Fake API as built; each case
    the port drops, with its reason.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (the requirements as failing checks first; audit a suite);
    - skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task; skill:review at each Task's close;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:diagnose when a test fails unexplained;
    - the project's `effect-api-documentation` skill for every Effect API.
tasks
    T62
        title       Package layout and import rules
        status      done
        priority    high
        description
            Fix the package's folders and what may import what, enforced by lint, before the tooling is built.

            **Why now:** tooling, fixtures and tests are about to be written. With no rule, tests reach into `src/`
            and fixtures into tests, which is how the old suite grew a private path to the runtime.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (section 8 and
            decision 9), code:tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md.

            May change: `vite.config.ts`, `tools/flow-state-lint/`, `tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md`, AGENTS.md's
            "Where things live". Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a rule that never fires → caught by its planted violation in
            code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts.
        acceptance
            - Lint encodes the package's top folders and what may import what between them: the core (everything
              in `src/` outside `src/host/`), the host, `fixtures/`, `tests/` and `bench/`. It does not encode the
              shape inside a folder. This Task moves no file: each folder is created by the Task that fills it
              (@task.V3.T63 the test tooling and the first fixture folder, @task.V3.T64 `tests/rules/`,
              @task.V3.T66 `bench/`, @task.V3.T67 the other fixture folders, @task.V3.T68 `tests/types/`).
            - Lint refuses, for `.ts` and `.tsx` files: anything in `src/` outside `src/host/`, except `src/index.ts`,
              importing from `src/host/`; `src/` importing a fixture, test or bench; a fixture importing from `src/`
              anything but `src/index.ts` and `src/host/testing/index.ts`; a test or bench importing from `src/`
              anything but those two, `src/host/inspect.ts` and `src/host/trace.ts`.
            - Each rule has a planted violation it refuses and a permitted import it allows.
            - `nub run check`, `nub run lint:rules` and `vp test` pass.
