    T64
        title       Rules checked on every run, and a reload at every step
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T63]
        description
            Write the run rules and the reload sweep in `tests/rules/`.

            **Why now:** example tests check only what someone wrote down: the planted fault `refused-turn-reported`
            passes all 81 hand cases. The old suite's crash sweep, a kill and reload at every step, found three real
            bugs and was deleted with it.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (sections 3.2, 3.3
            and 6), code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts, and
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/bridge/checks/publication.ts for an older check's logic.

            May change: `tests/rules/`, and the Story tests that call the helper. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a rule that never fires → each rule is shown red on one planted fault.
            Gates: `nub run faults`, which rejects every named fault in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts.
        acceptance
            - A rule is a function from a finished run to its breaches, named by its Spec id. One helper applies every
              rule to a run, and every Story test calls it.
            - The rules: an Attempt's ending is delivered at most once (WriteLanes I15, I16); every ending has one of
              the three channels and a never-sent Attempt ends only NotSent (WriteLanes I3); every request of one
              Attempt carries one idempotency key and one input (WriteLanes I6); at most one publication per turn
              (Turn I9); a refused turn leaves no Turn report (Turn I14).
            - The reload sweep runs every fixture story with a reload inserted at each position and applies the rules.
              A variant fails only for a rule breach, never for a script reason.
            - `nub run faults` catches every named fault, the 17 there today included.
    T65
        title       A run prints as a text trace
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T63]
        description
            Write `src/host/trace.ts`: one function from a finished run to plain text, showing each step, what it
            caused and each checkpoint.

            **Why now:** builders debugged the old suite with private scratch scripts, and a ruling is to be asked as
            two traces of one Story. This is the first slice of @plan.Inspection.O4; @task.V3.T49 keeps the rest.

            May change: `src/host/trace.ts`, `tests/transfers/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a trace that leaves out what a step caused → caught by a snapshot that shows each request,
            ending and store write of a run with a lost answer.
        acceptance
            - For one transfers Story with a lost answer and a reload, a test states by hand what the trace must
              show, in order: each step, each request with whether it landed, each ending with its channel and
              reason, each store write and each checkpoint.
            - Two runs of one Story print the same trace.
            - A text snapshot of that trace is kept as a change detector only.
