    T67
        title       The hand cases run as Story tests and the bridge is gone
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T63, @T64]
        description
            Port the 81 cases under `tests/bridge/cases/` to Story tests by Spec area, and delete the bridge.

            **Why now:** two test styles in one tree is how a private harness comes back. Core work
            (@task.V3.T54) waits on this.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md (section 5 and
            Appendix A), code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/bridge/cases/write-lanes/payment-endings.test.ts.

            **Approach:** the pay, cells, sync and sign-in fixtures in the four-file shape first. Then one Spec area
            per commit, each commit deleting the bridge files it replaces. The ten long scripts on the branch
            `draft/story-slice` (under `draft/workloads/`) become each fixture's usual and long stories.

            May change: `fixtures/`, `tests/`, `vite.config.ts` (the bridge's lint exemption). Evidence: this Task's
            comments.

            False pass: a ported test that asserts less than its case did → caught by comparing asserted values case
            by case, and by `nub run faults`.
        acceptance
            - Every bridge case has a Story test asserting the same values; a case dropped is listed with its reason.
            - `tests/bridge/` and `fixtures/part.ts` are deleted, and lint's bridge exemption with them.
            - The five known bugs that have a reproduction (Appendix A) are inverted tests, each titled by the rule it
              breaks.
            - Each fixture has a usual and a long story.
            - `nub run faults`: every named fault caught, and a dead core fails every test that is not inverted.
            - The suite's coverage record (Covers, Suite, Rerun, Mutants, Audit, Matched at, Scope, as
              skill:policy-verification gives them) is a comment on this phase, proposed to the user as a
              verification entry of @plan.Runtime. The audit it names runs at the phase's close, after
              @task.V3.T70.
